                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "28482641",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197981019190",
                            "num_reviews": 89,
                            "playtime_forever": 18,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 18,
                            "last_played": 1482224348
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Being a PC gamer, I've grown used to poor ports. It's a sad fact that in today's gaming industry consoles are considered first when it comes to new releases, with PC being a tacked-on afterthought held together by ducktape, snot and wishful thinking. \n\nSpace Rift breaks the mold by being a poor PC port... of a PC game. Starting with the unskippable opening sequence (Don't you just love those?), continuing to catastrophic controls (with both gamepad and mouse/keyboard) and finishing off with clipped screen edges, poor explanations of its control scheme and an overall feeling that this is not a game as much as a shameless moneygrab riding on the success of the VR version. \n\nDon't buy this game, don't play this game, don't even mention this game in polite society.",
